-- title:
--   A primitive root generates the field of all roots of unity
-- statement:
--   Let $M/K$ be any field extension, let $m\ge1$, and let $\zeta\in M$ be a primitive $m$-th root of unity. Then
--
--   $$
--   K(\zeta)=K(\{b\in M:b^m=1\}).
--   $$
--
--   No algebraicity assumption on the ambient extension $M/K$ is required.
--
--   This identifies the field generated by one primitive root with the field generated by all roots of the same order.
--
